---
import '../../styles/global.css';
import AcademicsNavbar  from '../../components/AcademicsNavbar.astro';
import AcademicsFooter from '../../components/AcademicsFooter.astro';
  
const lastUpdated = 'August 2026';
---

<html lang='en'>
  <head>
    <meta charset='UTF-8' />
    <meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0' />
    <title>Privacy Policy | SPMH Academics & Internships</title>
  </head>
  <body class='bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 antialiased'>
    <AcademicsNavbar />

    <main class='max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-20'>
      <div class='mb-10 space-y-2'>
        <h1
          class='text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight'>
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class='text-sm text-slate-500'>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <p class='text-sm text-slate-600'>
          This policy covers the Academics & Internships section of the St.
          Paul's Mission Hospital (SPMH) website, including the attachment
          application form, partnership inquiry form, and applicant status
          tracker.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class='prose prose-slate max-w-none space-y-10 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700'>
        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>
            1. Information We Collect
          </h2>
          <p>
            When you submit an attachment application, we collect your full
            name, email address, phone number, home institution, requested
            rotation or department, proposed attachment dates, and any details
            you include in your cover letter.
          </p>
          <p>
            When an institution submits a partnership inquiry, we collect the
            institution name, contact person, email address, institutional
            scope, and the details provided in the inquiry message.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>
            2. How We Use Your Information
          </h2>
          <ul class='list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5'>
            <li>
              To review and process attachment applications and partnership
              inquiries.
            </li>
            <li>
              To communicate with you about the status of your application,
              including through the reference code lookup on our Applicant
              Status Tracker.
            </li>
            <li>
              To coordinate scheduling and placement with the relevant SPMH
              department.
            </li>
            <li>
              To maintain institutional records as required for accreditation
              and audit purposes.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>
            3. How We Store Your Information
          </h2>
          <p>
            Application and inquiry data submitted through this section is
            stored in a secured database and is accessible only to authorized
            SPMH HR and Administration staff. We do not sell or rent your
            personal information to third parties.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>
            4. Your Reference Code
          </h2>
          <p>
            The reference code generated upon submission is the primary way you
            can check your application status without creating an account. Treat
            it as you would any personal identifier — avoid sharing it publicly,
            since anyone with the code can view the associated application
            status.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>5. Data Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We retain application and inquiry records for as long as necessary
            to support the attachment or partnership relationship, and
            thereafter as required for institutional record-keeping and
            regulatory compliance.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>6. Your Rights</h2>
          <p>
            You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of the
            personal information you have submitted by contacting our Human
            Resources Directorate using the details below.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>7. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about this policy or your data, contact SPMH Human
            Resources at
            <a
              href='mailto:hr@spmh.co.ke'
              class='text-blue-600 font-semibold underline'>hr@spmh.co.ke</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <p class='text-xs text-slate-400 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200'>
          This policy is a general institutional template and should be reviewed
          against applicable Kenyan data protection law (including the Data
          Protection Act, 2019) before being treated as final legal guidance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <AcademicsFooter />
  </body>
</html>
